  "claims":[
    {"claim_id":"C01","claim_text":"Git 2.28 documents git init -b/--initial-branch; if the name is omitted, the initial branch falls back to master. The current pinned git-init manual still documents -b. The page labels 100-130 minutes as an estimate, not measured learner timing, and the lab sets the local user.name and user.email that git commit describes as the usual authorship configuration.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","source":{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/v2.28.0/Documentation/git-init.txt","snapshot_digest":"sha256:64267d838b88492b3e4decb3594f8813b0b9058e337de143d49afe5772152128","locator":"git-init-2.28.txt lines 71-75","review_text_digest":"sha256:64267d838b88492b3e4decb3594f8813b0b9058e337de143d49afe5772152128"},"supporting_sources":[{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-init.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:123096436d7d47b718483fdfbc1660446474a77b2a5b33212f5360af89ca2f95","locator":"lines 15 and 78","review_text_digest":"sha256:123096436d7d47b718483fdfbc1660446474a77b2a5b33212f5360af89ca2f95"},{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-commit.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:ec670cfacaf3df8745e9cfe2fa68b74247cb111e4208e1a0095036732cb5e717","locator":"lines 529-539","review_text_digest":"sha256:ec670cfacaf3df8745e9cfe2fa68b74247cb111e4208e1a0095036732cb5e717"}]},
    {"claim_id":"C02","claim_text":"The Atlassian April 5, 2022 review says the event started at 7:38 UTC, the deletion API deleted a site when given a site ID, 883 sites representing 775 customers were deleted between 07:38 and 08:01 UTC, restoration took up to 14 days, and backups existed but this deletion still required manual extraction from shared stores. The page does not quote a delete-site label.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","source":{"retrieval_uri":"https://www.atlassian.com/blog/how-we-build/post-incident-review-april-2022-outage","snapshot_digest":"sha256:362a7f575942dee4f2d5227e9d71f237b013fbb5fbd45501e7401697f62461d5","locator":"review text lines 136, 147-148, 282, 365, and 431-434; snapshot_digest is the raw HTML, review_text_digest is the extracted text","review_text_digest":"sha256:2274460e87a671c425b3525b4ee87aa6b93a62e20b8e7fde3a082fcc515c8790"}},
    {"claim_id":"C03","claim_text":"git add puts the file contents present at that invocation into the index, the proposed next commit. git commit records the current index as a new commit that is a child of HEAD and moves the current branch to it.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","source":{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-add.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:42089b80b378a7e9711dde024b7ec94a6863378164ea434a34c6af07632e65db","locator":"lines 19-35","review_text_digest":"sha256:42089b80b378a7e9711dde024b7ec94a6863378164ea434a34c6af07632e65db"},"supporting_sources":[{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-commit.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:ec670cfacaf3df8745e9cfe2fa68b74247cb111e4208e1a0095036732cb5e717","locator":"lines 22-27","review_text_digest":"sha256:ec670cfacaf3df8745e9cfe2fa68b74247cb111e4208e1a0095036732cb5e717"}]},
    {"claim_id":"C04","claim_text":"Commit-form git reset moves HEAD to the named commit. The mode then decides whether the index and working tree change. The page teaches that commit form. Path-form reset is a different operation and is not what the page teaches.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","source":{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-reset.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:da477f7cc126877972c124922a9abc6417eaf3ac03ccadaf7743e3d4e85254d2","locator":"lines 33-45 and the state table at lines 407-412","review_text_digest":"sha256:da477f7cc126877972c124922a9abc6417eaf3ac03ccadaf7743e3d4e85254d2"}},
    {"claim_id":"C05","claim_text":"--soft leaves the index and working tree unchanged while moving HEAD. An immediate commit records that unchanged index as a new child commit, so the tree can match while the hash differs.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","source":{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-reset.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:da477f7cc126877972c124922a9abc6417eaf3ac03ccadaf7743e3d4e85254d2","locator":"lines 44-49 and table row --soft at lines 410-412","review_text_digest":"sha256:da477f7cc126877972c124922a9abc6417eaf3ac03ccadaf7743e3d4e85254d2"},"supporting_sources":[{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-commit.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:ec670cfacaf3df8745e9cfe2fa68b74247cb111e4208e1a0095036732cb5e717","locator":"lines 22-27","review_text_digest":"sha256:ec670cfacaf3df8745e9cfe2fa68b74247cb111e4208e1a0095036732cb5e717"}]},
    {"claim_id":"C06","claim_text":"--mixed is the default. It leaves the working directory unchanged and updates the index to the new HEAD, so the removed commit is no longer staged.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","source":{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-reset.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:da477f7cc126877972c124922a9abc6417eaf3ac03ccadaf7743e3d4e85254d2","locator":"lines 33-39 and table row --mixed at line 411","review_text_digest":"sha256:da477f7cc126877972c124922a9abc6417eaf3ac03ccadaf7743e3d4e85254d2"}},
    {"claim_id":"C07","claim_text":"--hard overwrites files and directories from the target, may overwrite untracked files, and removes tracked files that are not in the target. The page sentence that a scratch note may survive is the open side of that may, not a manual inventory of which untracked paths survive.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","source":{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-reset.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:da477f7cc126877972c124922a9abc6417eaf3ac03ccadaf7743e3d4e85254d2","locator":"lines 52-56","review_text_digest":"sha256:da477f7cc126877972c124922a9abc6417eaf3ac03ccadaf7743e3d4e85254d2"}},
    {"claim_id":"C08","claim_text":"git add records only the content present when it runs; a later edit is not in the index until another git add. A branch or reflog names commits, not those unstaged bytes. The page word blobs matches the index object model in rev-list --indexed-objects, which pretends the trees and blobs used by the index are listed.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","source":{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-add.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:42089b80b378a7e9711dde024b7ec94a6863378164ea434a34c6af07632e65db","locator":"lines 32-35","review_text_digest":"sha256:42089b80b378a7e9711dde024b7ec94a6863378164ea434a34c6af07632e65db"},"supporting_sources":[{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/rev-list-options.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:8414be814954bad98c510c44a5bbf477c07072b185c0c079600fceedf5f5b371","locator":"lines 957-960","review_text_digest":"sha256:8414be814954bad98c510c44a5bbf477c07072b185c0c079600fceedf5f5b371"}]},
    {"claim_id":"C09","claim_text":"Reflogs record reference-tip updates in the local repository. The default show action lists them, and the HEAD reflog also records branch switching. Those records are files under logs/ in the repository. The page statement that this history is not pushed is that locality; the catalog has no git-push manual.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","source":{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-reflog.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:59e7f0f15204a8c9f9b058ee62cb26aa2fa726b35dc85c702b75243424d6bf54","locator":"lines 27-42","review_text_digest":"sha256:59e7f0f15204a8c9f9b058ee62cb26aa2fa726b35dc85c702b75243424d6bf54"},"supporting_sources":[{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/gitrepository-layout.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:39ce8d137a30e1fd80eeae146b1c424e56f688f4ddd001259eb98543d3209439","locator":"lines 249-256","review_text_digest":"sha256:39ce8d137a30e1fd80eeae146b1c424e56f688f4ddd001259eb98543d3209439"}]},
    {"claim_id":"C10","claim_text":"ref@{n} selects the n-th prior reflog value, so a larger n is older and the selector requires $GIT_DIR/logs/<ref>. HEAD~n is a different selector: the n-th first-parent ancestor. The page tells the reader to confirm the reflog target before moving a branch.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","source":{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/revisions.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:b23a9eb17d9b193adccee6b79cb1c1fef450703dae925a33b8a1c6f6639d82ff","locator":"lines 101-108 and 163-168","review_text_digest":"sha256:b23a9eb17d9b193adccee6b79cb1c1fef450703dae925a33b8a1c6f6639d82ff"},"supporting_sources":[{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-reflog.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:59e7f0f15204a8c9f9b058ee62cb26aa2fa726b35dc85c702b75243424d6bf54","locator":"lines 30-31","review_text_digest":"sha256:59e7f0f15204a8c9f9b058ee62cb26aa2fa726b35dc85c702b75243424d6bf54"}]},
    {"claim_id":"C11","claim_text":"A commit found through the reflog can be given a new branch without switching to it, the current branch can be reset to it, or its change can be reapplied with cherry-pick. The page presents those three choices.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","source":{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-branch.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:6631281ad04c4afe0c348b0138fa0176f17b40fce37ef1e62c5e9f91235610cd","locator":"lines 59-68","review_text_digest":"sha256:6631281ad04c4afe0c348b0138fa0176f17b40fce37ef1e62c5e9f91235610cd"},"supporting_sources":[{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-reset.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:da477f7cc126877972c124922a9abc6417eaf3ac03ccadaf7743e3d4e85254d2","locator":"lines 395-405","review_text_digest":"sha256:da477f7cc126877972c124922a9abc6417eaf3ac03ccadaf7743e3d4e85254d2"},{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-cherry-pick.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:89c50911d1c5ca05148104bbd9e8daec79f3b109f2d41bc57ecb81076c4b4f7c","locator":"lines 18-20","review_text_digest":"sha256:89c50911d1c5ca05148104bbd9e8daec79f3b109f2d41bc57ecb81076c4b4f7c"}]},
    {"claim_id":"C12","claim_text":"Reachable reflog entries expire on gc.reflogExpire, default 90 days, and unreachable entries on gc.reflogExpireUnreachable, default 30 days. git gc prunes loose objects older than two weeks by default. The page states only the qualitative difference and the existence of grace periods.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","source":{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-reflog.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:59e7f0f15204a8c9f9b058ee62cb26aa2fa726b35dc85c702b75243424d6bf54","locator":"lines 111-127","review_text_digest":"sha256:59e7f0f15204a8c9f9b058ee62cb26aa2fa726b35dc85c702b75243424d6bf54"},"supporting_sources":[{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-gc.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:e3dbc4081095faf8d2d760eb4a47a1350f89d0c772f55eaada9cfbcdbeafba8c","locator":"lines 81-83","review_text_digest":"sha256:e3dbc4081095faf8d2d760eb4a47a1350f89d0c772f55eaada9cfbcdbeafba8c"}]},
    {"claim_id":"C13","claim_text":"git branch -d or -D deletes that branch and its reflog. git branch <name> <start> creates the branch and does not switch to it. The HEAD reflog records branch switching, so a prior checkout may still identify the deleted tip. The page says may.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","source":{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-branch.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:6631281ad04c4afe0c348b0138fa0176f17b40fce37ef1e62c5e9f91235610cd","locator":"lines 66-68 and 88-90","review_text_digest":"sha256:6631281ad04c4afe0c348b0138fa0176f17b40fce37ef1e62c5e9f91235610cd"},"supporting_sources":[{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-reflog.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:59e7f0f15204a8c9f9b058ee62cb26aa2fa726b35dc85c702b75243424d6bf54","locator":"line 41","review_text_digest":"sha256:59e7f0f15204a8c9f9b058ee62cb26aa2fa726b35dc85c702b75243424d6bf54"}]},
    {"claim_id":"C14","claim_text":"git revert records a new commit that reverses the selected change and leaves the original commit in history. The manual points reset --hard at discarding uncommitted work, which is a different operation. Choosing revert for shared history is the page collaboration rule built on that difference.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","source":{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-revert.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:63cd3400c56f2c55e61ac2d6048e72c0b700071caabe8d9b337a37d8b180b5fd","locator":"lines 17-29","review_text_digest":"sha256:63cd3400c56f2c55e61ac2d6048e72c0b700071caabe8d9b337a37d8b180b5fd"}},
    {"claim_id":"C15","claim_text":"git revert accepts --continue after a conflict, and the shared sequencer text says --continue resumes a failed revert or cherry-pick after the conflicts are resolved. The page says to stage the resolution and continue rather than switch to reset.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","source":{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-revert.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:63cd3400c56f2c55e61ac2d6048e72c0b700071caabe8d9b337a37d8b180b5fd","locator":"synopsis line 12 and line 75","review_text_digest":"sha256:63cd3400c56f2c55e61ac2d6048e72c0b700071caabe8d9b337a37d8b180b5fd"},"supporting_sources":[{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/sequencer.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:3cbd44896eff9db75ae2b61b378f5368139f3fbff4fac30b9cb116730f9ddd90","locator":"lines 1-4","review_text_digest":"sha256:3cbd44896eff9db75ae2b61b378f5368139f3fbff4fac30b9cb116730f9ddd90"}]},
    {"claim_id":"C16","claim_text":"git revert -m <parent> selects the mainline parent, numbered from 1. Later merges bring in only changes from commits that are not ancestors of the reverted merge. The faulty-merge howto shows that merging the updated side branch does not restore the reverted changes and does not un-join the histories. git merge prints Already up to date when every named commit is already an ancestor of HEAD. The page states the ancestry result and does not quote that porcelain string. Its usually for parent one follows the howto -m 1 example and is explicitly hedged.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","source":{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-revert.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:63cd3400c56f2c55e61ac2d6048e72c0b700071caabe8d9b337a37d8b180b5fd","locator":"lines 50-61","review_text_digest":"sha256:63cd3400c56f2c55e61ac2d6048e72c0b700071caabe8d9b337a37d8b180b5fd"},"supporting_sources":[{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/howto/revert-a-faulty-merge.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:fa45375bca469a8d9b756ce142b66572a2630540bd89e19b40c29560e7b158d9","locator":"lines 43-70","review_text_digest":"sha256:fa45375bca469a8d9b756ce142b66572a2630540bd89e19b40c29560e7b158d9"},{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-merge.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:8ef01610c3356215cd36ed18acf1fa460a7afbd8ac02b23b75d373b9765cece9","locator":"lines 157-158","review_text_digest":"sha256:8ef01610c3356215cd36ed18acf1fa460a7afbd8ac02b23b75d373b9765cece9"}]},
    {"claim_id":"C17","claim_text":"Without --staged, git restore reads the index into the working tree. With --staged, it reads HEAD into the index only. --source names a different tree for the working tree. The page replicas 1/2/3 contrast is that split.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","source":{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-restore.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:1d1ddfabee3ed19290f174e88b10884152b564048a8acd845b00074605e796d8","locator":"lines 21-40 and 56-61","review_text_digest":"sha256:1d1ddfabee3ed19290f174e88b10884152b564048a8acd845b00074605e796d8"}},
    {"claim_id":"C18","claim_text":"git checkout <tree> -- <path> replaces the worktree path from that tree and adds it to the index. git checkout -- <path> replaces the path from the index. The -- separates the path. The page no longer calls these the same destination as restore --source.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","source":{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-checkout.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:d20033febe92ef45146e054a64ea57e71922507618b8e3a94001f5079c5188bd","locator":"lines 75-93","review_text_digest":"sha256:d20033febe92ef45146e054a64ea57e71922507618b8e3a94001f5079c5188bd"}},
    {"claim_id":"C19","claim_text":"git restore --staged restores only the index, from HEAD by default, and leaves the working file. Pro Git names the resulting status sections: index versus HEAD is Changes to be committed, and index versus worktree is Changes not staged for commit.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","source":{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-restore.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:1d1ddfabee3ed19290f174e88b10884152b564048a8acd845b00074605e796d8","locator":"lines 25-26 and 59-61","review_text_digest":"sha256:1d1ddfabee3ed19290f174e88b10884152b564048a8acd845b00074605e796d8"},"supporting_sources":[{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/progit/progit2/a013e3230a1207cfa5ae94d28ba7d2021063c337/book/07-git-tools/sections/reset.asc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:88eb311f77bcebb89198e5c5e56d80407f4dd96840ba04470f1cf04629175696","locator":"lines 126 and 132","review_text_digest":"sha256:88eb311f77bcebb89198e5c5e56d80407f4dd96840ba04470f1cf04629175696"}]},
    {"claim_id":"C20","claim_text":"git cherry-pick applies the change from the named existing commit and records a new commit. It does not walk a range unless asked, so it does not merge the source branch. A new commit is a child of the current HEAD, so a different parent generally produces a different hash. The page diagram states that copy, not a moved source branch.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","source":{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-cherry-pick.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:89c50911d1c5ca05148104bbd9e8daec79f3b109f2d41bc57ecb81076c4b4f7c","locator":"lines 18-20 and 44-50","review_text_digest":"sha256:89c50911d1c5ca05148104bbd9e8daec79f3b109f2d41bc57ecb81076c4b4f7c"},"supporting_sources":[{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-commit.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:ec670cfacaf3df8745e9cfe2fa68b74247cb111e4208e1a0095036732cb5e717","locator":"lines 22-27","review_text_digest":"sha256:ec670cfacaf3df8745e9cfe2fa68b74247cb111e4208e1a0095036732cb5e717"}]},
    {"claim_id":"C21","claim_text":"If the patch does not apply, cherry-pick stops, leaves HEAD at the last successful commit, sets CHERRY_PICK_HEAD, and writes conflict markers. --continue resumes after the resolution is staged. The page also says to test the destination integration; that is teaching, not a manual requirement.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","source":{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-cherry-pick.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:89c50911d1c5ca05148104bbd9e8daec79f3b109f2d41bc57ecb81076c4b4f7c","locator":"lines 12-13 and 22-37","review_text_digest":"sha256:89c50911d1c5ca05148104bbd9e8daec79f3b109f2d41bc57ecb81076c4b4f7c"},"supporting_sources":[{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/sequencer.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:3cbd44896eff9db75ae2b61b378f5368139f3fbff4fac30b9cb116730f9ddd90","locator":"lines 1-4","review_text_digest":"sha256:3cbd44896eff9db75ae2b61b378f5368139f3fbff4fac30b9cb116730f9ddd90"}]},
    {"claim_id":"C22","claim_text":"Because cherry-pick does not traverse history, dependent commits have to be named in dependency order. A redundant commit stops under the default --empty=stop and is not recorded as an empty commit. An initially empty commit fails unless --allow-empty or --empty=keep is set. Creating a new branch leaves the experimental branch in place.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","source":{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-cherry-pick.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:89c50911d1c5ca05148104bbd9e8daec79f3b109f2d41bc57ecb81076c4b4f7c","locator":"lines 48-50 and 131-165","review_text_digest":"sha256:89c50911d1c5ca05148104bbd9e8daec79f3b109f2d41bc57ecb81076c4b4f7c"},"supporting_sources":[{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-branch.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:6631281ad04c4afe0c348b0138fa0176f17b40fce37ef1e62c5e9f91235610cd","locator":"lines 66-68","review_text_digest":"sha256:6631281ad04c4afe0c348b0138fa0176f17b40fce37ef1e62c5e9f91235610cd"}]},
    {"claim_id":"C23","claim_text":"git log --left-right --cherry-mark A...B uses the three-dot symmetric difference, prefixes the sides with < and >, and marks patch-equivalent commits with =. git-log includes the rev-list options that define those flags.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","source":{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/rev-list-options.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:8414be814954bad98c510c44a5bbf477c07072b185c0c079600fceedf5f5b371","locator":"lines 280-282 and 1231-1234","review_text_digest":"sha256:8414be814954bad98c510c44a5bbf477c07072b185c0c079600fceedf5f5b371"},"supporting_sources":[{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/revisions.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:b23a9eb17d9b193adccee6b79cb1c1fef450703dae925a33b8a1c6f6639d82ff","locator":"lines 307-312","review_text_digest":"sha256:b23a9eb17d9b193adccee6b79cb1c1fef450703dae925a33b8a1c6f6639d82ff"},{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-log.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:67e2e76723555409941d7a67d501d44e835a98a657fa71fbba664bda74255305","locator":"line 120 include of rev-list-options","review_text_digest":"sha256:67e2e76723555409941d7a67d501d44e835a98a657fa71fbba664bda74255305"}]},
    {"claim_id":"C24","claim_text":"The decision framework matches the command contracts: restore changes selected paths, reset moves local branch state and then the selected trees, revert adds an inverse commit for shared history, and cherry-pick copies selected changes. The inspect-before-and-after habit is the page procedure around those contracts.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","source":{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-reset.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:da477f7cc126877972c124922a9abc6417eaf3ac03ccadaf7743e3d4e85254d2","locator":"lines 33-56","review_text_digest":"sha256:da477f7cc126877972c124922a9abc6417eaf3ac03ccadaf7743e3d4e85254d2"},"supporting_sources":[{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-restore.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:1d1ddfabee3ed19290f174e88b10884152b564048a8acd845b00074605e796d8","locator":"lines 17-26","review_text_digest":"sha256:1d1ddfabee3ed19290f174e88b10884152b564048a8acd845b00074605e796d8"},{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-revert.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:63cd3400c56f2c55e61ac2d6048e72c0b700071caabe8d9b337a37d8b180b5fd","locator":"lines 17-29","review_text_digest":"sha256:63cd3400c56f2c55e61ac2d6048e72c0b700071caabe8d9b337a37d8b180b5fd"},{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-cherry-pick.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:89c50911d1c5ca05148104bbd9e8daec79f3b109f2d41bc57ecb81076c4b4f7c","locator":"lines 18-20","review_text_digest":"sha256:89c50911d1c5ca05148104bbd9e8daec79f3b109f2d41bc57ecb81076c4b4f7c"}]},
    {"claim_id":"C25","claim_text":"The four hands-on fences, executed unchanged in a disposable repository, create the base plus three feature commits, git reset --hard HEAD~3 leaves only the base commit and removes hpa.yaml, HEAD@{1} is the CPU-threshold commit, git reset --hard HEAD@{1} returns that same tip, and cherry-picking feature-scaling~1 then feature-scaling adds those two changes on main as new commits while deployment.yaml stays the base file and the source tip stays put. This is the lead practice-frozen execution on this page digest with git 2.56.0, not a rerun by this verifier.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","source":{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-reset.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:da477f7cc126877972c124922a9abc6417eaf3ac03ccadaf7743e3d4e85254d2","locator":"lines 52-56 and table line 412","review_text_digest":"sha256:da477f7cc126877972c124922a9abc6417eaf3ac03ccadaf7743e3d4e85254d2"},"supporting_sources":[{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/revisions.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:b23a9eb17d9b193adccee6b79cb1c1fef450703dae925a33b8a1c6f6639d82ff","locator":"lines 101-108 and 163-168","review_text_digest":"sha256:b23a9eb17d9b193adccee6b79cb1c1fef450703dae925a33b8a1c6f6639d82ff"},{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-cherry-pick.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:89c50911d1c5ca05148104bbd9e8daec79f3b109f2d41bc57ecb81076c4b4f7c","locator":"lines 18-20","review_text_digest":"sha256:89c50911d1c5ca05148104bbd9e8daec79f3b109f2d41bc57ecb81076c4b4f7c"},{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-reflog.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:59e7f0f15204a8c9f9b058ee62cb26aa2fa726b35dc85c702b75243424d6bf54","locator":"lines 38-42","review_text_digest":"sha256:59e7f0f15204a8c9f9b058ee62cb26aa2fa726b35dc85c702b75243424d6bf54"}]},
    {"claim_id":"C26","claim_text":"The three diagrams illustrate reset movement, revert ancestry, and a cherry-pick copy. The reset diagram says --hard moves HEAD and resets the index and working files, --mixed moves HEAD and resets the index, and --soft moves HEAD only. Conceptual hashes are labeled illustrative. The three-tree nickname and its collection-of-files limit are the Pro Git wording.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","source":{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-reset.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:da477f7cc126877972c124922a9abc6417eaf3ac03ccadaf7743e3d4e85254d2","locator":"lines 407-412","review_text_digest":"sha256:da477f7cc126877972c124922a9abc6417eaf3ac03ccadaf7743e3d4e85254d2"},"supporting_sources":[{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/progit/progit2/a013e3230a1207cfa5ae94d28ba7d2021063c337/book/07-git-tools/sections/reset.asc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:88eb311f77bcebb89198e5c5e56d80407f4dd96840ba04470f1cf04629175696","locator":"lines 9-22 and 206-210","review_text_digest":"sha256:88eb311f77bcebb89198e5c5e56d80407f4dd96840ba04470f1cf04629175696"}]},
    {"claim_id":"C27","claim_text":"Client-strategy kubectl apply prints the object that would be sent and does not send it. In kubectl 0.35 apply.go, info.Get runs before the DryRunClient branch, a non-NotFound Get error is returned as a from-server failure, and both Create and the patch path are skipped for DryRunClient. The command builds its REST mapper and namespace from the kubeconfig loader, whose default flag value is an empty kubeconfig path and whose loader starts from the default loading rules. The page separates this command from the Git fragments and requires a complete manifest. The lead run of these exact command bytes did not persist the complete Deployment.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","source":{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kubernetes/kubectl/v0.35.0/pkg/cmd/apply/apply.go","snapshot_digest":"sha256:47c02f5b5205c0f97a0e85a74eca22551077b769173b5a0ed59f728fab2c1898","locator":"lines 302-310 and 680-728","review_text_digest":"sha256:47c02f5b5205c0f97a0e85a74eca22551077b769173b5a0ed59f728fab2c1898"},"supporting_sources":[{"retrieval_uri":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/kubectl/generated/kubectl_apply/","snapshot_digest":"sha256:e7c42433e36cebc167402ea54913fda5d8c8bd033a5c455302c57f53b426d4ba","locator":"review text line 962; snapshot_digest is raw HTML","review_text_digest":"sha256:c61a6bce42bc081625263898746a74eb4737e80e3e9a6c636ac489397aff4d76"},{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kubernetes/cli-runtime/v0.35.0/pkg/genericclioptions/config_flags.go","snapshot_digest":"sha256:95fe3a6fd09a8fecde25a2501d6e80b89d843737be16f5ba17993425533634da","locator":"lines 160-167 and 477","review_text_digest":"sha256:95fe3a6fd09a8fecde25a2501d6e80b89d843737be16f5ba17993425533634da"}]},
    {"claim_id":"C28","claim_text":"git show includes the pretty formats and diff options. The default omitted format is medium. For a merge commit, that format prints a Merge: line of ancestral hashes before Author:. --summary adds a condensed header summary of creations, renames, and mode changes; it is not itself the parent printer. The page command git show --summary <hash> therefore shows both.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","source":{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/pretty-formats.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:43bb165e33cc8b269a34b664ebc874d6df0e0df66e887f655e257a3138cd5705","locator":"lines 4-8","review_text_digest":"sha256:43bb165e33cc8b269a34b664ebc874d6df0e0df66e887f655e257a3138cd5705"},"supporting_sources":[{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/pretty-options.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:5b46b922ccbf747793d29265eb8a0a5c060d010d4d00c6fe5e1e5ba2d45819b4","locator":"line 12","review_text_digest":"sha256:5b46b922ccbf747793d29265eb8a0a5c060d010d4d00c6fe5e1e5ba2d45819b4"},{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/diff-options.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:f12f2f624417476cf050ca067263be9f5122eb6dc800f09796044975d9046303","locator":"lines 294-296","review_text_digest":"sha256:f12f2f624417476cf050ca067263be9f5122eb6dc800f09796044975d9046303"},{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-show.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:91dfc431d85e53a12ef7854cbeb52674f4e2e52a7fe9ffe3ee018c1b2ed5ea30","locator":"lines 42-55 includes","review_text_digest":"sha256:91dfc431d85e53a12ef7854cbeb52674f4e2e52a7fe9ffe3ee018c1b2ed5ea30"}]},
    {"claim_id":"C29","claim_text":"Both git revert and git cherry-pick require a clean working tree with no modifications from HEAD. The page says to inspect git status and start clean before either command.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","source":{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-revert.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:63cd3400c56f2c55e61ac2d6048e72c0b700071caabe8d9b337a37d8b180b5fd","locator":"lines 19-20","review_text_digest":"sha256:63cd3400c56f2c55e61ac2d6048e72c0b700071caabe8d9b337a37d8b180b5fd"},"supporting_sources":[{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-cherry-pick.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:89c50911d1c5ca05148104bbd9e8daec79f3b109f2d41bc57ecb81076c4b4f7c","locator":"lines 19-20","review_text_digest":"sha256:89c50911d1c5ca05148104bbd9e8daec79f3b109f2d41bc57ecb81076c4b4f7c"}]},
    {"claim_id":"C30","claim_text":"Pro Git calls HEAD, the index, and the working directory the three trees, and defines tree there as a collection of files, not the Git tree object. HEAD is the last commit, the index is the proposed next commit, and the working directory is the sandbox. The page uses that name and states the worktree-versus-index limit.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","source":{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/progit/progit2/a013e3230a1207cfa5ae94d28ba7d2021063c337/book/07-git-tools/sections/reset.asc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:88eb311f77bcebb89198e5c5e56d80407f4dd96840ba04470f1cf04629175696","locator":"lines 9-22","review_text_digest":"sha256:88eb311f77bcebb89198e5c5e56d80407f4dd96840ba04470f1cf04629175696"}},
    {"claim_id":"C31","claim_text":"In a shared repository, receive.denyNonFastForwards is on by default, so a non-fast-forward push is rejected. When the current branch is an ancestor of the named commit, a fast-forward moves HEAD and the index without a merge commit. The page's hedged pair, a push may be rejected or may reintroduce removed commits, is that contrast.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","source":{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-init.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:123096436d7d47b718483fdfbc1660446474a77b2a5b33212f5360af89ca2f95","locator":"lines 137-139","review_text_digest":"sha256:123096436d7d47b718483fdfbc1660446474a77b2a5b33212f5360af89ca2f95"},"supporting_sources":[{"retrieval_uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/a018953688f1b10bddf91bff8747068f5f4746a4/Documentation/git-merge.adoc","snapshot_digest":"sha256:8ef01610c3356215cd36ed18acf1fa460a7afbd8ac02b23b75d373b9765cece9","locator":"lines 163-172","review_text_digest":"sha256:8ef01610c3356215cd36ed18acf1fa460a7afbd8ac02b23b75d373b9765cece9"}]}
